{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The nakedness of your son's daughter, etc.</b> Scripture speaks of the daughter of his raped woman, and his daughter and his son's daughter from his wife we learn from ״עֶרְוַת אִשָּׁה וּבִתָּהּ״, which is stated about them ״לֹא תְגַלֵּה״ — whether she is from him [his own daughter] or from another man (ibid. 22)." "<b>The nakedness of your son's daughter.</b> An a fortiori argument to your daughter — but since they do not give warning from a logical inference, they learn it from a gezerah shavah in tractate Yevamot (page 3a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:57.757826251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}